course: dictionary
lesson: 7862
title: Railings and the words around them
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A railing is a fence or barrier made of metal or wooden bars. It stops people falling, often on stairs, bridges and balconies. Railing is a noun, so you can have one railing or several railings.
explain: «Always hold the railing when you walk down the stairs.» Hold tells you what a railing is for: something to grip so you stay steady. «Never stand on a chair or climb anything on a balcony, because you could fall over the railing.» The clue is fall over: the railing is there to stop that.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Cross on the bridge, not on its railings.» Try "fence" instead of "railings": the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Railings are for holding and leaning on safely, not for climbing.
fact: A railing is a fence or barrier made of metal or wooden bars.
fact: A railing can also be a single bar you can hold on to, like a handrail.
fact: Railings often stand along stairs, bridges and balconies to stop people falling.
fact: «Salt from sea spray makes iron railings rust faster.» Railings by the sea rust quickly.
fact: Phrases to know: hold the railing, lean on the railing, iron railings.
exercise: «Always hold the railing when you walk down the stairs.» What is a railing? | A ball thrown in games | A step that goes up | *A bar or fence that helps keep you safe | A kind of bird
exercise: «Never stand on a chair on a balcony, because you could fall over the railing.» What is the railing there to stop? | The sun from shining | The chair from moving | *You falling | The rain from coming in
exercise: «Cross on the bridge, not on its railings.» Should you climb on the railings? | *No, you should hold them and stay safe | Yes, if you are in a hurry | No, because they are too shiny | Yes, it is fun to climb them
test: «Salt from sea spray makes iron railings rust faster.» Why do railings by the sea rust quickly? | They are painted every day | The sun is too hot | *Salt from sea spray | They are made of wood
test: «Cross on the bridge, not on its railings, and never jump off a bridge into water.» What should you do with the railings? | Climb over them | Use them as a slide | *Hold them for safety | Sit on them to rest
exam: Ella says a railing is a type of stair step. What does railing really mean? | A way of crossing water | *A fence or bar that stops people falling | A flat step for climbing | A loud noise from a bridge
